    thinking: "**Analyzing Korean Specification**\n\nI\'m currently diving into the user\'s Korean specification, specifically the document titled \"**[\354\265\234\354\242\205 \355\206\265\355\225\251 \352\270\260\355\232\215\354\204\234] AI \352\270\260\353\260\230 \354\243\274\354\260\250 \352\263\265\354\234\240 \354\204\234\353\271\204\354\212\244 \355\206\265\355\225\251 CS \352\264\200\353\246\254 \355\224\214\353\236\253\355\217\274**.\" I am currently examining the precise requirements, specifically the requested features, components, and the information contained in the image mockup. My immediate focus is on extracting and translating the critical information related to the project\'s features and functionality.\n\n\n**Extracting UI Component Details**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the design aspect, examining the UI mockup and detailed specs. I\'m focusing on dissecting each component, particularly the left sidebar, top bar, and the three-column workspace. I\'m working to understand the function of each element, from the side navigation to the interaction pad and customer profile form. My main goal is to fully understand the features and functions described in the design, and how they contribute to the overall user experience.\n\n\n**Defining Core Features**\n\nI am now drilling down into the core features. I\'m focused on the right column\'s resolution status and action items, specifically the status badges, canned replies, and action items list. I\'m also looking into the normalization of phone and car numbers, with the goal of ensuring robust search functionality. I\'m examining the UI of these components to extract relevant details about how the information will be used, and how it will improve the user experience.\n\n\n**Developing Customer Interactions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a new customer match popup. I need to display information, like the current agent\'s badge, progress, blacklist warnings, and special notes. I\'m also including a \"Takeover\" button that updates the agent\'s name in real time. Also, I\'m working to display a timeline of consultation logs and STT summaries for this specific customer. I need to integrate AI with this popup, so I\'m also working on that aspect.\n\n\n**Mapping Data Entities**\n\nI\'m now identifying and mapping the relevant data entities. I am focusing on the structures of `internal_agents`, `saved_templates`, `call_logs`, `consultations`, `agent_tasks`, and the archived `consultations_archive` table, noting their relationships and critical fields. I\'m prioritizing the fields related to customer information, agent details, and the consultation workflow for a holistic view.\n\n\n**Defining Server-Side Architecture**\n\nI\'m now determining the server setup. I have decided to configure a full-stack custom server with Express. I will leverage the existing framework instructions to guide this process. I\'m reviewing the `package.json` scripts and making sure that these scripts contain the proper build and dev command to use express, along with `esbuild`. The goal is to fully understand the necessary setup for integrating the Gemini API.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 105293721
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
