  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Architecture Components**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the initial architectural components. The current plan is to use a `src/types/index.ts` file to hold shared TypeScript interfaces and enums. My priority is to create the `Customer` interface for now, following the specification\'s modular approach. This will kickstart a structured approach to the project.\n\n\n**Outlining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now outlining key data structures. I\'ve drafted interfaces and types for `InternalAgent`, `SavedTemplate`, `CallLog`, `Consultation`, `AgentTask`, and `ParkingSpot`. They will be added to the `src/types/index.ts` file, building upon the initial `Customer` interface. I\'m also planning utilities to normalize phone numbers and car numbers, which will be added to `src/lib/utils/normalize.ts`. This effort is ensuring data consistency.\n\n\n**Developing Service Modules**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial service modules. I\'m focusing on `sttService.ts` for CTI call simulation and transcript handling, and `aiSummaryService.ts` for AI summary generation, which utilizes the server route `/api/ai/summarize`. I\'m also developing `customerService.ts` for customer lookup, agent takeover, and archive management.\n\n\n**Defining API Integration**\n\nI\'m now defining the API integrations. I\'m focusing on server-side calls using the Gemini API (`@google/genai` with `gemini-3.6-flash`) for real-time STT summary and key issue extraction. I\'m also planning `/api/ai/briefing` for the morning briefing, `/api/ai/recommend-parking`, and `/api/cti/calls` to simulate the call log list.\n\nI\'m also working on developing the frontend components. I\'ve specified `src/components/SideNavBar.tsx`, `src/components/TopNavBar.tsx`, `src/components/search/HeaderSearchBar.tsx`, `CustomerTimelineModal.tsx`, and `src/components/workspace/LeftInteractionPad.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing Workspace Components**\n\nI\'m now designing the crucial workspace components. I\'ve broken down `CenterCustomerForm.tsx`, which will hold customer and car details, including a detailed car type selector and account information with a verified badge and parking recommendations. I\'m building `RightTaskManager.tsx` for resolution status tags, canned responses, and Google Tasks-style action items. Furthermore, `CalendarView.tsx` will display a hybrid calendar with parking hope dates, tasks, and color-coded statuses. I\'m working to integrate these features for an efficient workflow.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 771752330
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
