  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Consultation Logging**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the initial data capture phase of our consultation logging process. The key is to ensure the phone number and vehicle inquiry details are correctly logged and saved in the database right from the start. I want to optimize this process, making sure it is as streamlined as possible.\n\n\n**Addressing Data Overwrites**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the root cause: the `handleSaveLog` function in `App.tsx` was updating a single consultation object instead of creating new entries. This was overwriting existing customer and vehicle details with new phone numbers and car information. I\'m focusing on ensuring each consultation log is a distinct entity and that the form resets correctly after each save.\n\n\n**Clarifying New Log Creation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"\354\203\201\353\213\264 \353\241\234\352\267\270 \354\240\200\354\236\245 & DB\354\240\200\354\236\245\" action. It\'s clear that each click needs to trigger a *new* `Consultation` item in the `consultations` array, complete with a unique ID and all relevant details. This should also ensure new customer records are created or linked. Crucially, the input form should reset after each save to enable swift handling of subsequent inquiries. This should fix the single-card display on the Kanban board.\n\n\n"
