  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Visualizing Kanban Cards**\n\nI\'m exploring how to enhance Kanban cards. I\'m thinking of displaying customer phone numbers and car numbers directly on the cards. Specifically, I\'m considering using a concise format like \"\360\237\232\227 [car number] ([phone number])\" within the \"cons\" section, prioritizing the car number if available. This should provide quick access to key contact information.\n\n\n**Enhancing Consultation Records**\n\nI\'ve realized a significant improvement: directly incorporating `car_number` and `phone_number` within the `Consultation` interface. This ensures each saved consultation retains an explicit snapshot of the contact information used at the time of the log\'s creation. Now, I\'m considering how this affects data retrieval and display in Kanban cards.\n\n\n**Refining Consultation Data Capture**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the `handleSaveLog` function efficiently captures consultation details. It creates a new `Consultation` record with critical information, including the customer\'s car number and phone number, at the moment of the interaction. Then, it resets the input form for the next customer. The next step is updating the Kanban card display to make it immediately useful.\n\n\n**Organizing Kanban Card Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating consultation data fields directly onto the Kanban cards for clarity. I\'m focusing on displaying key information: car number, phone number, parking location, status, sub-status, summary, and agent name. I\'ve realized that each saved registration will now create its own independent Kanban card under the relevant status, which should resolve the previous issue.\n\n\n**Clarifying Data Persistence Logic**\n\nI\'ve clarified the save log mechanism: each \"\354\203\201\353\213\264 \353\241\234\352\267\270 \354\240\200\354\236\245\" click ALWAYS creates a NEW consultation entry, prepending it to the `consultations` state. New customer data is added, or existing customer data is updated, in the `customers` state, and the form resets. Each saved consultation gets its own independent Kanban card, ensuring no data overwrites occur.\n\n\n**Implementing Kanban Card Details**\n\nI\'m now implementing the display of phone and car numbers at the top of Kanban cards for easy distinction. I\'m focusing on updating `src/types/index.ts` to include `car_number` and `phone_number` in the `Consultation` interface. I\'m also updating mock data in `src/lib/mockData.ts` to include these fields. Finally, I\'m refactoring the `handleSaveLog` function in `src/App.tsx` to ensure new customer and consultation objects include the correct data, appending to the `consultations` array.\n\n\n**Resetting Data Entry Form**\n\nI\'m now implementing the final form reset after saving a consultation log. After saving a consultation, I\'m resetting `selectedCustomer` to a blank customer profile and also resetting the `notes` field. I\'m also adding a notification confirming the save. In addition, I\'m adding a \"\354\213\240\352\267\234 \354\203\201\353\213\264 \354\236\221\354\204\261 (\354\236\205\353\240\245 \354\264\210\352\270\260\355\231\224)\" button to the main hub. This button triggers the form reset manually.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 69381456
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
