    thinking: "**Analyzing Customer Interactions**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the implications of an agent\'s action: clicking \"\354\203\201\353\213\264 \353\241\234\352\267\270 \354\240\200\354\236\245 & DB \354\246\211\354\213\234 \353\223\261\353\241\235.\" My focus is on the data flow. Specifically, I am considering the scenarios where a user enters a phone number and car number with varying status options. I am digging into how these entries trigger database updates and downstream processes.\n\n\n**Defining New Consultation Objects**\n\nI\'ve outlined the instantiation of a `Consultation` object when the \"\354\203\201\353\213\264 \353\241\234\352\267\270 \354\240\200\354\236\245 & DB \354\246\211\354\213\234 \353\223\261\353\241\235\" action is triggered. My emphasis is on data integrity, specifically how the new consultation data is constructed, including the handling of customer details, derived statuses, and timestamping. I\'m ensuring consistency in the data model and validating all critical elements.\n\n\n**Implementing Form Reset Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the form reset functionality after a new consultation is saved. My focus is on ensuring a clean slate for the next customer interaction. This involves creating a fresh `newCustomerRecord` object, resetting all form fields, and defaulting the workspace status to \'\354\240\221\354\210\230\'. I\'m also adding a dedicated \"Reset Form\" button to the `MainConsultationHub` component for easy access.\n\n\n**Refining Active Consultation Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the derivation of `activeConsultation` within `App.tsx`. The current logic, specifically lines 58-61, has me concerned. There\'s a potential fallback to `consultations[0]` if `selectedCustomer.id` is new, which isn\'t ideal. I\'m considering maintaining an `activeConsultationId` or a local draft consultation state. This allows status and sub-status modifications in the form to dynamically update the current draft consultation. I am currently evaluating implementing local draft states for `status`, `sub_status`, and `parkingName` using `useState`.\n\n\n**Defining Consultation Data Flow**\n\nI\'m now concretizing the data flow when an agent saves a consultation. The updates to `draftStatus` and `draftSubStatus` are integral for updating the current form. Clicking \"\354\203\201\353\213\264 \353\241\234\352\267\270 \354\240\200\354\236\245 & DB \354\246\211\354\213\234 \353\223\261\353\241\235\" triggers the creation of a *new* `Consultation` object within the `consultations` array, complete with a unique ID and data derived from the current draft and user selections. This ensures that *every* save creates a distinct record in the database, like the examples given.\n\n\n"
