  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding New Features**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `handleSaveAndNotify` function within `MainConsultationHub.tsx`. I\'m focusing on how it currently calls `onSaveLog(notes)`. A new button is also planned, labeled \"\354\213\240\352\267\234 \354\236\205\353\240\245 (\354\264\210\352\270\260\355\231\224)\". This should be conveniently located next to the existing save button, or within the card header for quick access.\n\n\n**Refining Save Functionality**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into how `handleSaveLog` functions within `App.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m analyzing how it handles the creation of new database entries upon \"\354\203\201\353\213\264 \353\241\234\352\267\270 \354\240\200\354\236\245 & DB \354\246\211\354\213\234 \353\223\261\353\241\235\" clicks, and how it resets the form. The goal is to ensure that a fresh, independent entry is generated and that the form clears appropriately after each save. I\'m focusing on the interaction between `handleSaveLog` and the `selectedCustomer` state, making sure phone and car data are snapshotted.\n\n\n**Generating New Consultation**\n\nI am currently working to ensure that the creation of new consultation records is always performed without overwriting existing entries. I am generating new, unique IDs for each consultation using a timestamp and a random number to avoid conflicts. The `newConsultation` object will use the `customerId`, car number, phone number, and other data for the new entry. I\'m focusing on ensuring these entries are independent and preserve past data.\n\n\n**Implementing Form Reset**\n\nI\'ve incorporated a `handleResetForm` function, which now generates a fresh `Customer` object. This function resets form inputs to their defaults by calling the `setSelectedCustomer` and `setNotes` functions. I\'ve also added an `onResetForm` prop to `MainConsultationHubProps` and connected it to the new functionality in the App.tsx file.\n\n\n**Analyzing Consultation Status**\n\nI am now investigating the `handleChangeStatus` function within `App.tsx` and how it interacts with the `activeConsultation` state. I\'m focusing on ensuring changes to consultation status and sub-status are handled correctly. Furthermore, I need to make sure the reset function for a new consultation, which clears customer data like phone number and car number, does not interfere with updating or displaying consultation status.\n\n\n**Drafting Consultation Objects**\n\nI\'m now implementing a fallback draft `activeConsultation` object to handle new or reset customers. I\'m ensuring this draft incorporates `selectedCustomer` data, including car number and phone number, and assigns a unique `id` like \"draft-[customer ID]\". This setup maintains data integrity while displaying a suitable placeholder for new or unassigned consultations. I\'m focusing on ensuring the draft object\'s `status` and `sub_status` are set to reasonable defaults.\n\n\n**Defining Consultation Creation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the system creates new consultations, particularly in response to status changes, saving, and draft scenarios. The process always creates a permanent consultation object, including handling draft scenarios. My current work involves tracing how the `handleSaveLog` function interacts with the `handleChangeStatus` function when saving or when draft IDs are present. This ensures that new consultation entries are correctly created with unique identifiers using `cons-${Date.now()}` and are properly prepended to the `consultations` array, regardless of draft or saved status, or whether the status has been changed in the UI before a save. I\'m focusing specifically on how different statuses are handled and ensuring the logic covers all edge cases.\n\n\n**Validating Consultation Logic**\n\nI\'m currently validating the logic for creating and saving new consultations. I\'ve tested scenarios where a new consultation is initiated, saved, and then a subsequent one is created. The system correctly generates unique IDs for each consultation and appends them to the `consultations` array, as expected. The Kanban board accurately displays both entries with their respective data, confirming the independence of each new record. I\'m focusing on ensuring data integrity and preventing overwrites in all scenarios.\n\n\n"
