flicts**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing a critical issue: the sub-status field not updating correctly, especially for draft consultations or when directly editing the sub-status. It turns out the root cause is how the `setConsultations` function handles synthetic `activeConsultation` objects or those not yet in the array. Specifically, the problematic behavior stems from the conditional logic where `setConsultations` does not perform an update if the `activeConsultation` isn\'t found in the previous consultations. I\'m now implementing the approach to solve this, and the need to double-check places where `activeConsultation` and `selectedConsultationId` are managed.\n\n\n**Defining Edit Flow**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the intended edit workflow. My focus is on ensuring a clear distinction between updating existing consultations and creating new ones, especially regarding the \'\354\235\264\354\226\264\354\204\234 \354\210\230\354\240\225\' option. I\'m ensuring `selectedConsultationId` is correctly set on Kanban card clicks, and properly derived from history cards and the `customers` list. Updates to `selectedConsultationId` should update `activeConsultation` correctly, and also automatically switch to the workspace. Furthermore, I\'ll ensure customer details are correctly loaded and displayed upon selection or click.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI enhancements in `MainConsultationHub.tsx`. I\'ve added badges and status indicators above the save button and form header. If `activeConsultation` exists, I\'m displaying \"\342\234\217\357\270\217 [\352\270\260\354\241\264 \354\203\201\353\213\264 \354\210\230\354\240\225 \353\252\250\353\223\234]\" along with the ID and changing the save button text to \"\360\237\222\276 \352\270\260\354\241\264 \354\203\201\353\213\264 \354\210\230\354\240\225 \353\202\264\354\232\251 \354\240\200\354\236\245\". There is also an option for creating a new consultation for the same customer. For new entries, the badge says \"\360\237\206\225 [\354\213\240\352\267\234 \354\203\201\353\213\264 \353\223\261\353\241\235 \353\252\250\353\223\234]\", and the button says \"\360\237\222\276 \354\213\240\352\267\234 \354\203\201\353\213\264 \353\241\234\352\267\270 DB \354\240\200\354\236\245\".\n\n\n"
