  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Missing Functionality**\n\nI\'ve isolated a critical issue in `MainConsultationHub.tsx`. Lines 604-643 are relevant; the displayed customer history cards lack the required edit functionality within the `visibleCustomerConsultations` view, specifically the \"\354\235\264 \354\203\201\353\213\264 \355\216\270\354\247\221\355\225\230\352\270\260\" button. I am also investigating related code in `KanbanBoardView.tsx` to understand the full context.\n\n\n**Refining Consultation Editing**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the core of the editing workflow. The cards lack a button, I\'m going to add an `onSelectConsultation` method that will allow continuous editing, not the generation of a new item. I\'m focusing on the state management in `App.tsx` using `selectedConsultationId: string | null` and `activeConsultation`. Next, I will address the persistent issue with the sub-status reason input field.\n\n\n**Implementing Consultation Logic**\n\nI\'ve been working on consultation selection and fallback mechanisms. The logic now prioritizes finding a consultation by `selectedConsultationId`, and falls back to searching by customer ID and ensuring the consultation isn\'t \'\354\231\204\353\243\214\' status. If no existing consultation is found, I\'m generating a draft consultation object.\n\n\n**Defining Consultation Behavior**\n\nI\'m now detailing the behavior of selecting consultations. My focus is on the `handleSelectConsultation` method. When triggered, I first locate the selected consultation, and then use the matching `consId` to update `selectedConsultationId`. If I find an existing consultation, I\'m setting the `selectedCustomer` and notes, and finally switching the view to the workspace tab to allow for immediate edits.\n\n\n**Updating Consultation Records**\n\nI\'m now implementing the logic for updating or creating consultations. I\'m focusing on the `consultations` array. If a matching ID exists, I\'m updating the existing consultation with new data, ensuring that I merge any new fields, such as `car_number`, `phone_number`, and `summary`. If the consultation doesn\'t exist, I\'ll add a new one. I\'m leveraging `setConsultations` and map to handle the updates effectively.\n\n\n**Adding New Consultation Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating logic for the \"\354\213\240\352\267\234 \354\203\201\353\213\264 \354\266\224\352\260\200 \354\236\221\354\204\261\" button. It resets the `selectedConsultationId` to null, clears the notes, and generates a fresh draft. I\'m also addressing the persistent sub-status reason input issue. When the `handleChangeStatus` function is called, I\'m updating either the existing consultation in the `consultations` array or a draft record, ensuring accurate state management. This avoids duplication and allows continuous editing.\n\n\n**Refining Status Updates**\n\nI\'ve refined the `handleChangeStatus` function to handle immediate updates. The input box now smoothly updates state for both existing and draft consultations. I\'ve ensured that new status values, along with the optional `subStatusReason`, are correctly applied to the `consultations` array or, if a draft, correctly added to the array. The code ensures seamless and continuous updates.\n\n\n**Improving State Management**\n\nMy recent efforts have focused on stabilizing state management during status and sub-status changes. I\'ve eliminated the sub-status input freeze by ensuring drafts are added/updated in the `consultations` array. I also defined the `handleChangeSubStatus` handler to ensure `activeConsultation` state is properly handled. I\'m leveraging explicit event handlers for improved data flow.\n\n\n**Integrating Consultation Events**\n\nI\'m now integrating the event handlers for consultation selection across the UI. I\'m focusing on handling clicks on Kanban cards in `KanbanBoardView.tsx` and customer history cards in `MainConsultationHub.tsx`. In `KanbanBoardView.tsx`, I\'ve added an `onSelectConsultation` prop to update the state and switch to workspace. Similarly, I\'m adding `onSelectConsultation` and `onStartNewConsultation` to `MainConsultationHub.tsx` to enable seamless transitions to editing.\n\n\n"
