    thinking: "**Defining Consultation Props**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the props for `MainConsultationHub`. I\'ve added `onSelectConsultation`, `onStartNewConsultation`, and `isExistingConsultation`. I\'m going to review the interplay of `activeConsultation` next to ensure seamless functionality.\n\n\n**Synchronizing State Updates**\n\nI\'ve been working through the logic for updating state when a consultation is selected. Specifically, I\'m integrating the `notes`, and `sub_status` state variables to reflect the chosen consultation, in `App.tsx`. I\'m also synchronizing the `selectedCustomer` state, making sure it corresponds to the chosen `consultation`. If there is no matching customer, I\'m creating a new customer object.\n\n\n**Implementing New Consultation Flows**\n\nI\'m now implementing the handlers for new consultation flows. I\'ve added `handleStartNewConsultation` to reset the consultation ID and clear notes. Additionally, `handleResetForm` clears customer data and resets the consultation ID, setting me up to start fresh. I\'m making sure these functions are properly integrated and tested.\n\n\n**Analyzing Save Log Function**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `handleSaveLog` function within `App.tsx`. I\'m focused on how it updates customer records and handles the interaction between the `selectedCustomer` and the `activeConsultation`. I\'m carefully reviewing the logic to ensure that customer data is updated correctly and the corresponding consultation is updated. I need to make sure the data flow is as expected.\n\n\n**Updating Consultation Records**\n\nI\'m now implementing the update logic for existing consultations and new consultation flows, within the `handleSaveLog` function. I\'m focusing on how I can update an existing consultation when data changes and how I can create a new consultation when required, ensuring the necessary state variables are updated and saved correctly. I\'m also ensuring that updated consultations are preserved.\n\n\n**Refining Data Persistence**\n\nI\'m currently working to integrate new consultations within `handleSaveLog`, focusing on ensuring the new consultation is correctly added to the state. I\'m prioritizing data persistence in the `consultations` array, including adding a new consultation ID after its creation. I\'ve also integrated the `handleChangeStatus` function to handle updates efficiently.\n\n\n**Evaluating Status Updates**\n\nI\'m now deep in the update logic, specifically the `handleChangeStatus` function. I\'m focusing on the direct mutation of the `consultations` array when editing an existing consultation, handling status and sub-status changes directly. I\'ve analyzed the logic that allows for persistent updates and the flow of updates to the array.\n\n\n**Validating State Synchronization**\n\nI\'m now thoroughly examining the state updates within `MainConsultationHub.tsx`, specifically how input typing affects the `sub_status`. I\'ve made changes to ensure the `consultations` array state always reflects changes to input fields like `sub_status`, guaranteeing real-time updates without issues. I\'m focusing on validating these recent updates.\n\n\n**Visualizing Editing Modes**\n\nI\'m now integrating a clear status badge in `MainConsultationHub.tsx` to differentiate between editing existing consultations and starting new ones. The badge will clearly display the consultation ID, and it will give the user an option to start a new consultation using this customer\'s data, which enhances usability. The changes are intended to streamline user experience.\n\n\n**Clarifying UI Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now implementing visual cues and interactions in the UI. I\'ve added a status badge that distinguishes between new and existing consultations. I\'ve also modified the save button text dynamically based on the consultation status. Lastly, I\'m integrating an \"Edit\" button into the customer history list, which improves accessibility.\n\n\n**Refining Consultation Selection**\n\nI\'m now refining how consultations are selected, focusing on the UI/UX. Clicking either a button or a card now selects it, using an onClick handler to trigger the `onSelectConsultation` prop. I\'m also ensuring the selected consultation is clearly highlighted using styling, distinguishing it from unselected consultations, based on whether its ID matches the active one.\n\n\n**Enhancing Kanban Card Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating improvements to the Kanban board card interactions within `KanbanBoardView.tsx`. I\'m focusing on refining the edit functionalities and adding a status display. I want the `handleEditConsultation` function to update the existing consultation state when an \"Edit\" button is clicked and ensure changes are saved properly.\n\n\n**Integrating Card Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now integrating enhanced card interactions within `KanbanBoardView.tsx` to streamline the user experience. The full card and a dedicated button now trigger consultation selection, using `onSelectConsultation`. I\'ve added a button with an edit icon that utilizes `e.stopPropagation()` to prevent conflicts. I\'m focusing on ensuring these additions seamlessly handle consultation updates and selection.\n\n\n**Validating UX Improvements**\n\nI\'m now making final checks on recent component edits. Specifically, I\'m validating that the `onSelectConsultation` prop is correctly used within both `KanbanBoardView.tsx` and `MainConsultationHub.tsx`. I\'m confirming user interactions trigger consultation selection and ensure the `activeTab` switches to `\'workspace\'` after, displaying the consultation and customer data for editing.\n\n\n**Updating Kanban Card Logic**\n\nI\'m now incorporating changes to the Kanban board cards. I\'m focusing on the \"\342\234\217\357\270\217 \354\235\264\354\226\264\354\204\234 \354\210\230\354\240\225\" button, and have added an `onSelectConsultation` prop to `MainConsultationHub` and `KanbanBoardView`, ensuring that card clicks correctly invoke consultation selection. I\'m also implementing the `handleSelectConsultation` function in `App.tsx` and verifying reliable interactions.\n\n\n"
