s includes updating an existing consultation, if one exists, or creating a new one with the customer\'s details.\n\n\n**Examining Consultation Updates**\n\nI\'m now focused on how consultations are updated or created within `handleSaveLog`. I\'m tracing the logic that conditionally updates an existing consultation with new data, or creates a fresh consultation if one doesn\'t exist. Specifically, I see the function taking values from `activeConsultation` for default values when a new consultation is created, such as `parking_name`, `inquiry_type`, `status` and others. I\'m focusing on the mapping of the new data and how values are derived.\n\n\n**Investigating Status Changes**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on `handleChangeStatus`. I\'ve observed it updates a consultation\'s `status` and `sub_status`. The logic involves finding the target consultation\'s index. If found, a new array is returned with the updated entry. If it is not found, a new draft consultation is created and inserted into the consultations array to persist the sub-status update seamlessly.\n\n\n"
