    thinking: "**Defining User Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently meticulously organizing the user\'s three key requirements and formulating an implementation strategy. Specifically, I\'m focusing on making the \"new input initialization\" the default value, and considering implications on other aspects.\n\n\n**Analyzing Database Logic**\n\nI\'m now delving into the database interaction logic. My current focus is how to handle existing records upon phone or car number input. If a match is found, I intend to automatically connect the existing customer data. This would include auto-connecting the relevant recent consultation record, for quick access. This should automatically shift into a \"review/edit\" mode.\n\n\n**Refining Data Handling**\n\nI\'ve successfully updated the data handling process. If a match is found in the database by phone or car number, I provide guidance indicating the existing data has been loaded and is ready for modification. In the absence of a match, the system ensures a new mode is available, supporting new entries seamlessly. Also, I made sure that incomplete vehicle information, such as empty fields for car number, car type, or detailed car type, is valid for saving, thus facilitating note-taking or scenarios with unknown data. My key adjustments involve ensuring empty string values are acceptable for car-related fields in storage and handler logics.\n\n\n"
